@startuml
title Instagram comment and DM automation — implemented modules

left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}

class "InstagramWebhookRoutes" as Routes <<HTTP routes>> {
  +GET /api/webhooks/instagram
  +POST /api/webhooks/instagram
  +POST /api/webhooks/instagram/subscription
  +verifyWebhookSignature(rawBody, signature)
}

class "WebhookEvents" as Events <<normalizer>> {
  +normalizeCommentEvents(payload)
}

class "ProcessIncomingMessage" as Incoming <<automation>> {
  +processIncomingMessage(event, dependencies)
}

class "ProcessComment" as Processor <<automation>> {
  +processComment(event, dependencies)
}

class "DeliverReply" as Delivery <<automation>> {
  +deliverReply(input, dependencies)
}

class "AccountRepository" as Accounts <<persistence>> {
  +findByInstagramUserId(id)
}

class "AutomationRepository" as Automations <<persistence>> {
  +findEnabledByAccountAndMedia(accountId, mediaId)
}

class "ExecutionRepository" as Executions <<persistence>> {
  +claimExecutions(deliveries)
  +markDispatchStarted(id, leaseId)
  +markSucceeded(id, leaseId, replyId)
  +markRetryPending(id, leaseId, failure)
  +markFailed(id, leaseId, failure)
  +markUncertain(id, leaseId, failure)
}

class "DmConversationRepository" as Conversations <<persistence>> {
  +recordInboundAnswer(answer)
  +claimFollowup(id, now, leaseUntil)
  +claimDueFollowups(now, leaseUntil, limit)
  +markFollowupSucceeded(id, leaseId, replyId)
}

class "TokenProtector" as Tokens <<security>> {
  +decrypt(ciphertext)
}

class "InstagramCommentReplyClient" as PublicClient <<Meta adapter>> {
  +replyToComment(input)
}

class "InstagramPrivateReplyClient" as PrivateClient <<Meta adapter>> {
  +sendPrivateReply(input)
}

class "DeliverFollowup" as Followup <<automation>> {
  +deliverFollowup(claim, dependencies)
}

class "InstagramDirectMessageClient" as DirectClient <<Meta adapter>> {
  +sendDirectMessage(input)
}

class "InstagramWebhookClient" as Subscription <<Meta adapter>> {
  +subscribeToComments(input)
}

class "Maintenance" as Maintenance <<scheduled>> {
  +runMaintenance(dependencies)
}

Routes --> Events : normalizes signed delivery
Routes --> Processor : each comment event
Routes --> Incoming : each supported inbound DM
Routes --> Subscription : enables comments and optional messages
Processor --> Accounts : finds account
Processor --> Automations : finds matching rule
Processor --> Executions : claims channel executions
Processor --> Delivery : dispatches claimed executions
Incoming --> Accounts : finds recipient account
Incoming --> Conversations : saves answer and claims follow-up
Incoming --> Followup : dispatches claimed follow-up
Delivery --> Tokens : decrypts token
Delivery --> Executions : records attempt and outcome
Delivery --> PublicClient : public channel
Delivery --> PrivateClient : private channel, optional quick replies
Followup --> Tokens : decrypts token
Followup --> Conversations : records attempt and outcome
Followup --> DirectClient : recipient-addressed DM
Maintenance --> Delivery : retries eligible executions
Maintenance --> Followup : retries eligible follow-ups

note bottom of Events
  Supported inbound text and quick-reply messages are processed.
  Other signed messaging events are counted as unsupported.
end note

@enduml
